# Local testing
- Start test servers with OTP logging and a separate port, so no real SMS is sent (the dev database may have Message Central selected; real SMS went out once):
  ```bash
  cd apps/api && OTP_PROVIDER=log PORT=4100 nohup pnpm exec tsx src/server.ts > ~/.cache/grocery-build/api-test.log 2>&1 &
  ```
- Stop every server you started before finishing (`pkill -f "tsx src/server.ts"`, then check with `pgrep`).
- Seed accounts: `admin@grocery.test` and `staff@grocery.test`, password `grocery-dev`. Customer `+919000000002`, partner `+919000000004` (OTP in the API log).
- WSL memory is limited: run one heavy build at a time (Next.js build, Docker build) and write logs to `~/.cache/grocery-build/`, not `/tmp` (WSL restarts wipe it).

# Production VPS (test client "moozy")
- Connect with `ssh grocery-vps` (key-based, `deploy` user with passwordless sudo). The stack is in `~/moozy/deploy`; domains are `api.moozy.in` and `admin.moozy.in`.
- Deploy after the developer pushes:
  ```bash
  ssh grocery-vps 'cd ~/moozy && git pull && cd deploy && docker compose up -d --build'
  ```
  1 CPU: about 5 minutes. Don't poll it repeatedly; check once with `docker compose ps`.
- Never print values from `deploy/.env` or `deploy/api.env`; show variable names only. Never ask for passwords in chat.
- Before anything destructive on the server (deleting volumes, data, containers), back up, explain, and get confirmation.
